# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Chairman ruling R7, 15 September 2026: "ship the four headers and short
# HSTS; CSP is a separate item." The four content/referrer/frame/permissions
# headers have no lock-in on a static site. HSTS is deliberately short
# (7 days) with no preload and no includeSubDomains for the first rollout;
# lengthen it once a cycle has passed without incident.
#
# Content-Security-Policy (enforced) is NOT written here: it is appended to
# the `/*` block of dist/_headers at build time by
# scripts/build/csp-hashes.mjs (postbuild), because its script-src carries a
# sha256 hash of every executable inline <script> the build renders, and
# three of those are Astro's own runtimes that change on any upgrade. Chairman
# direction, 11 October 2026, in-session: "all and then merge it". Inventory:
# .council/research/2026-09/csp-inline-script-inventory-2026-09-17.md.
# Never add an inline on*= attribute in src/ — the policy disables it and the
# build refuses it. `npm run audit:static` lints the built file.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=604800

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
